	// Bond Bonds name bond0, bond1, … in declaration order (independent of the entry's position in the network array); vlan.link references that name. params speak kernel names (miimon, lacp_rate, …) — cloud-init v2/netplan spellings (mii-monitor-interval, lacp-rate, arp-ip-targets, …) are accepted and folded onto the canonical names; the same key declared twice under two spellings rejects, unknown keys reject. Multi-value targets (arp-ip-targets) take a JSON array. params without miimon or arp_interval get the default miimon=100 — the kernel's own default since v4.18 (older kernels default to 0: link monitoring off); a declared arp_interval is ARP monitoring and excludes miimon. The declared bonds are cross-checked against the live system after install (INSTALL_BOND_MISMATCH on member/mode/miimon drift).
